      slug: "sts-lasting",
      title: "6 · Thirty years on the sideline: lasting is its own achievement",
      section: "Section 2 · The road",
      body: `A course that only celebrates debuts will miss the rarer thing, which is duration.

**Pam Oliver's route.** Florida A&M, where she was an AIAW All-American in the 400 meters and part of the university's first women's national championship team. Local news in Georgia, then ESPN, then FOX Sports from 1995, starting on the network's number-one NFL crew alongside Pat Summerall and John Madden. Three decades later she was still working NFL sidelines through the 2025 season, and FOX bills her as the longest-tenured NFL sideline reporter in the business (FOX Sports, n.d.). Her honors include a Gracie Award in 2018, WISE Woman of the Year in 2008, the Association for Women in Sports Media's Mary Garber Pioneer Award, induction into the National Association of Black Journalists Hall of Fame in 2020, and induction into the Sports Broadcasting Hall of Fame in December 2025 (Sports Broadcasting Hall of Fame, n.d.).

**Why duration is harder than a debut.** A debut requires one decision by one employer. Lasting requires surviving every reorganization, every rights change, every new executive with a new idea, and every year of a body doing a physically demanding job in thirty different buildings. Roughly thirty NFL Sundays a year for thirty years is the purest version of the itinerant contractor problem: the parking, the credential, the flight, the hotel, the mileage, the deductible, absorbed as friction rather than tracked as cost.

**The reframe this course wants.** Road cost is not friction. It is a line item, and an untracked line item is a pay cut you administer to yourself. Someone working a thirty-venue season has thirty sets of documented expenses, and the difference between recording them and remembering them is money.

**The honest note.** Oliver's move off FOX's number-one NFL crew in 2014 is a real and widely discussed episode in her career. It is also a living person's professional grievance that this course's research pass did not verify, so the course does not characterize it. Naming a subject you have not researched is worse than omitting it.

:::reveal Why is lasting thirty years in this job a rarer achievement than a debut? ||| A debut needs one decision by one employer. Lasting means surviving repeated reorganizations, rights changes, new executives, and the physical cost of working roughly thirty venues a season for three decades.

:::reveal What does this lesson mean by calling untracked road cost a self-administered pay cut? ||| Travel, parking, mileage and per-venue expenses are deductible business costs. Absorbing them as friction instead of recording them means the contractor pays them out of income that could have been offset.

## Vocabulary
- **Sideline reporter**: the broadcaster working at field level for in-game reporting, interviews and injury updates.
- **Tenure**: unbroken length of service in a role, which is a separate professional claim from being first to hold it.
- **Line item**: a cost recorded individually so it can be counted, billed or deducted.
- **Itinerant contractor**: a self-employed worker whose job happens at a different client site each engagement.

## Sources
FOX Sports. (n.d.). *Pam Oliver*. https://www.foxsports.com/presspass/bios/on-air/pam-oliver

Sports Broadcasting Hall of Fame. (n.d.). *Pam Oliver*. https://www.sportsbroadcastinghalloffame.org/inductees/pam-oliver/`,
